# Repository Licensing

This repository is a monorepo. Each component may have a different license.
Watch carefully which component you use and which license applies to it.

Before using, copying, modifying, distributing, or incorporating any part of
this repository into another project, identify the component and verify its
applicable license in the table below, in that component's directory, and in
any accompanying license or notice file.

## Component and license list

| Component or path | Applicable license | License text or notice |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `<component-or-path>` | `<license>` | `<path-to-license-or-notice>` |
| `<component-or-path>` | `<license>` | `<path-to-license-or-notice>` |

Add every separately licensed component to this table. Do not assume that the
license of one component applies to another component.

## Default license

Unless a component, directory, file, or accompanying notice explicitly states
that a different license applies, the original code in this repository is
licensed under the MIT License below.

This default does not relicense third-party code, dependencies, generated code,
bundled assets, or other material that is identified as belonging to another
copyright holder. Those materials remain subject to their respective licenses.

